	abstract = {Although the number of sites making eddy covariance CO2 flux measurements throughout the world has increased rapidly over the last two decades it is still a challenge to define and build a new system. There are myriad options for tower design and placement and a steadily growing range of instrument options and configurations. Selecting among these options is based on finding an optimal solution that best achieves the precision and accuracy required to satisfy the scientific objectives for a site and often for the lowest installation and operational costs. Site design is only the first step to ensuring accuracy and precision of the results.},
